/* Help articles for the on-site guide. Generated by scripts/build_solutions.py; do not edit. */
window.BF_KB = [{"q":"How do I start?","a":"Open Studio and choose a worked example close to your field, or create a table and paste your data straight from Excel or an instrument export. Then press Analyze, or open Facet for a suggestion.","l":"studio/","t":"Getting started","k":"getting started"},{"q":"Which table type should I use?","a":"XY for curves and spectra (one X column, one or more Y columns; columns with the same title are replicates). Column for comparing groups. Multiple variables for compositions, process settings and properties, one row per sample.","l":"studio/","t":"Getting started","k":"getting started"},{"q":"Can I import instrument files?","a":"Yes. Drop them anywhere on Studio, or choose Import files to pick several at once. Supported: Excel (.xlsx), CSV, TXT, XY, JCAMP-DX, PANalytical XRDML, Rigaku RAS, Bruker UXD, Thermo SPC, and CIF (which becomes a simulated XRD pattern). Export binary .raw or .brml scans as .xy or .xrdml first. Files are read in the browser and never uploaded.","l":"studio/","t":"Getting started","k":"getting started"},{"q":"Do I need an account?","a":"No. Everything runs in your browser and projects are kept there. There is no account yet: Pro is activated on each computer with an access code we send you. Accounts with cloud storage are planned.","l":"studio/","t":"Getting started","k":"getting started"},{"q":"Which equation should I fit?","a":"Run Auto-fit: it fits every plausible equation for the shape of your data and ranks them by AICc. Equation discovery can also find a formula that is not in the library.","l":"tools/curve-fitting/","t":"Curve fitting and equations","k":"curve fitting and equations"},{"q":"The fit does not converge.","a":"Check that X and Y are in the right columns and units, try Auto-fit, fix a parameter you know, or start from a simpler model. Very few points cannot support many parameters.","l":"tools/curve-fitting/","t":"Curve fitting and equations","k":"curve fitting and equations"},{"q":"Can I type my own equation?","a":"Yes. Choose User-defined equation and write it with x, any parameter names, + − * / ^ and functions such as exp, ln and sqrt.","l":"tools/curve-fitting/","t":"Curve fitting and equations","k":"curve fitting and equations"},{"q":"Which test should I use?","a":"Facet suggests one from your data: t test or Mann–Whitney for two groups, ANOVA, Welch’s ANOVA or Kruskal–Wallis for more. Lattent checks normality and equal variance for you.","l":"studio/?example=anova","t":"Statistics","k":"statistics"},{"q":"Why not several t tests?","a":"Each extra test raises the chance of a false positive. ANOVA with Tukey or Holm–Šidák post tests corrects for the number of comparisons.","l":"studio/?example=anova","t":"Statistics","k":"statistics"},{"q":"How is crystallite size calculated?","a":"Peaks are fitted with pseudo-Voigt profiles on a fitted baseline, instrumental broadening is removed, and the Scherrer and Williamson–Hall equations give size and strain. Sizes above about 100 nm are unreliable with any lab diffractometer.","l":"tools/xrd-crystallite-size/","t":"XRD, spectra and band gaps","k":"xrd, spectra and band gaps"},{"q":"How do I identify the phase?","a":"After a peak analysis with X as 2θ, press Identify phases and list the elements that may be present. Lattent matches your peaks against every computed structure of those elements.","l":"tools/xrd-crystallite-size/","t":"XRD, spectra and band gaps","k":"xrd, spectra and band gaps"},{"q":"My Tauc fit looks wrong.","a":"Choose the transition type (direct or indirect) and set the linear region by hand around the steepest part of the absorption edge.","l":"tools/xrd-crystallite-size/","t":"XRD, spectra and band gaps","k":"xrd, spectra and band gaps"},{"q":"What can Facet do without an API key?","a":"Suggest analyses, check the whole project for mistakes, read data from a picture of a graph and write the report. All of this runs offline in your browser.","l":"ai/","t":"Facet and the AI models","k":"facet and the ai models"},{"q":"How do I use the chat?","a":"Open Facet, press Add AI key and paste your own Anthropic or OpenAI key; it stays in your browser. Type a question at the foot of the panel, or attach a figure and ask what it shows or what is wrong with it. Analyses it proposes run only after you approve them.","l":"ai/","t":"Facet and the AI models","k":"facet and the ai models"},{"q":"How accurate are the models?","a":"Each model’s accuracy on data it never saw is listed on the AI page and the validation page.","l":"ai/","t":"Facet and the AI models","k":"facet and the ai models"},{"q":"The database search fails.","a":"Discover queries the public Alexandria database from your browser. Check your connection, or a network that blocks external sites, and try again; very broad searches can be slow.","l":"studio/?discover=search","t":"Discover: database, phases, new materials","k":"discover: database, phases, new materials"},{"q":"Are generated materials real discoveries?","a":"They are candidates: compositions predicted to be stable and close to your target band gap, and absent from the database. Confirm them with a calculation or a synthesis.","l":"studio/?discover=search","t":"Discover: database, phases, new materials","k":"discover: database, phases, new materials"},{"q":"How do I get a figure for my paper?","a":"Every chart has PNG export. Pro adds Journal size, which draws the figure at the exact column width and text size for ACS, RSC, Elsevier, Nature or Wiley and saves it as TIFF, PNG or vector SVG without the watermark, plus methods, results and figure-legend text written from your numbers.","l":"studio/","t":"Figures, reports and export","k":"figures, reports and export"},{"q":"Can I analyse many files at once?","a":"Yes. Choose Import files and select them all (or drop them on Studio); each becomes a table. Run the analysis on one, set the options, then choose Run on other tables. Every table gets its own analysis, and the key numbers are collected in one summary table you can plot against the temperature or time in the file names. Free plans run batches of up to 5 files.","l":"studio/","t":"Figures, reports and export","k":"figures, reports and export"},{"q":"Can I export my results?","a":"Yes: results tables as CSV and one-page reports with Pro, and your data tables as CSV on any plan.","l":"studio/","t":"Figures, reports and export","k":"figures, reports and export"},{"q":"Where is my project saved?","a":"In your browser, automatically. Clearing the browser’s site data removes it, so keep important work as a project file (Save file) or as a share link.","l":"account/","t":"Projects and sharing","k":"projects and sharing"},{"q":"How does the Lab plan work?","a":"The Lab plan covers up to ten people on one invoice. Each member activates Pro with their own access code, and projects are shared by link or as files. Shared cloud workspaces are planned.","l":"account/","t":"Projects and sharing","k":"projects and sharing"},{"q":"How do I pay?","a":"Request a payment link or an invoice from the contact page. We send a Lemon Squeezy link (card, worldwide) or a Razorpay link (UPI and cards, India) within a working day, and an access code once payment is confirmed. Online checkout is being set up.","l":"pricing/","t":"Plans and billing","k":"plans and billing"},{"q":"I paid, but Pro is still locked.","a":"Your access code arrives by email once the payment is confirmed, usually the same day. Activate it on the Account page with the email address it was issued to. If it has not arrived within a working day, write to us with your receipt.","l":"pricing/","t":"Plans and billing","k":"plans and billing"},{"q":"How do I cancel or get a refund?","a":"Write to us; you keep Pro until the end of the paid period. Refunds within 14 days of a payment, no questions asked.","l":"pricing/","t":"Plans and billing","k":"plans and billing"},{"q":"My pasted data lands in one column.","a":"Lattent recognises tab, comma and semicolon separators and decimal commas. If the paste still lands in one column, copy the cells directly from Excel rather than from a PDF, or use Paste or import.","l":"support/","t":"Troubleshooting","k":"troubleshooting problem error broken"},{"q":"A chart is blank or the page looks broken.","a":"Use a recent Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari, reload the page, and turn off extensions that block scripts for this site.","l":"support/","t":"Troubleshooting","k":"troubleshooting problem error broken"},{"q":"Studio is slow with a large file.","a":"Curve fitting and AutoML work best with up to a few thousand points; for long spectra, crop to the region of interest first.","l":"support/","t":"Troubleshooting","k":"troubleshooting problem error broken"},{"q":"I lost my project.","a":"Projects live in the browser where you made them. If the browser’s data was cleared and the project was not kept as a file or a share link, it cannot be recovered.","l":"support/","t":"Troubleshooting","k":"troubleshooting problem error broken"},{"q":"What can I do with Lattent?","a":"Lattent is a workspace for analysing lab data in your browser. Paste or import measurements (XRD, UV–Vis, Raman, FTIR, isotherms, kinetics, tensile tests, assay plates or any table), then fit curves with 35 built-in equations, run statistics with the checks built in, fit peaks, and get crystallite size, band gap, activation energy and more. Every result comes with uncertainties, a publication figure and methods text. Discover adds a database of 5.8 million computed materials, XRD phase identification and generative design; Facet, the AI lab partner, suggests and checks analyses. Nothing is installed and your data stays on your computer.","l":"studio/","t":"Open Studio","k":"lattent overview capabilities features do does purpose use about introduction what is explain describe summary offer"},{"q":"Who is Lattent for?","a":"Researchers and students in materials science, chemistry, chemical engineering and physics: anyone who measures XRD, spectra, isotherms, kinetics or mechanical properties and needs fits, statistics and figures for a paper, thesis or report. Teaching labs use it because there is nothing to install and the free plan has every analysis.","l":"solutions/","t":"Solutions by field","k":"who audience users student phd researcher scientist engineer teacher professor industry company academic university suitable"},{"q":"Which measurements and instruments does Lattent support?","a":"XRD from any diffractometer; UV–Vis, FTIR and Raman spectra; adsorption isotherms and kinetics; Arrhenius and VFT data; DSC crystallisation; tensile tests; Tafel plots from electrochemistry; plate assays (dose–response, enzyme kinetics, qPCR, standard curves); and any XY, column or multi-variable table.","l":"tools/","t":"Quick tools","k":"measurement measurements technique data type types kind supported handle xrd spectra uv vis ftir raman isotherm kinetics dsc tensile tafel electrochemistry assay plate reader instrument"},{"q":"Which analysis should I run?","a":"Press Suggest an analysis on any table: Lattent's shape model recognises the kind of behaviour (a spectrum, an absorption edge, a saturating isotherm, a thermally activated trend) and proposes the right analysis with one-click Run. Or press Analyze to choose from the full list, grouped into fitting, spectra and materials, statistics, and machine learning.","l":"studio/","t":"Open Studio","k":"which analysis choose suggest recommend right appropriate method model should pick decide"},{"q":"What is Lattent Studio?","a":"Studio is the main workspace. A project holds data tables, each table has its analyses, and each analysis has its results, graph and write-up. Everything updates when you edit a value. Projects are saved in your browser, and can be kept as a file or shared by link.","l":"studio/","t":"Open Studio","k":"studio workspace project table analysis what is"},{"q":"What is Discover?","a":"Discover is Lattent's materials side: search 5.8 million computed crystal structures (the Alexandria database) with 3D structures, simulated XRD patterns and CIF files; identify the phases in your XRD pattern; and generate new compositions with Lattent's own diffusion model, with predicted formation energy and band gap.","l":"studio/?discover=search","t":"Open Discover","k":"discover database materials crystal structure search alexandria phase generate what is"},{"q":"Can I open Excel files?","a":"Yes. Drop an .xlsx or .xlsm workbook on Studio or choose Import files. Every sheet with numbers becomes a table, a two-row header such as Temperature over K becomes Temperature (K), and hidden sheets are skipped. Old binary .xls files need saving as .xlsx or CSV first. Nothing is uploaded.","l":"studio/","t":"Open Studio","k":"excel xlsx xls spreadsheet workbook sheet import open"},{"q":"Can I analyse many files at once?","a":"Yes. Choose Import files and select them all (or drop them on Studio); each becomes a table. Run the analysis on one, set the options, then choose Run on other tables. Every table gets its own analysis, and the key numbers are collected in one summary table you can plot against the temperature or time in the file names. Free plans run batches of up to 5 files.","l":"studio/","t":"Open Studio","k":"batch bulk many multiple files series automate summary table run on other tables once"},{"q":"Can I export a figure at my journal's size?","a":"Yes. On any chart press Journal size, choose ACS, RSC, Elsevier, Nature, Wiley or a custom width, and the figure is drawn at that column width and text size, with a preview at printed size. Download it as TIFF, PNG with the resolution recorded, or vector SVG. Journal size is a Pro feature.","l":"pricing/","t":"See pricing","k":"journal size tiff column width acs rsc elsevier nature wiley figure export resolution dpi publication paper"},{"q":"How do I export my results and figures?","a":"Every chart has PNG export on the free plan. Pro adds SVG, 600-dpi PNG and journal-size TIFF without a watermark, results tables as CSV, one-page reports and project files. Data tables export as CSV on any plan.","l":"studio/","t":"Open Studio","k":"export download figure png svg tiff csv report results save"},{"q":"How do I share a project with a colleague?","a":"Press Share in Studio to get a link that carries a copy of the whole project (tables, analyses and graphs) inside the link itself; nothing is uploaded. Whoever opens it gets their own copy. For ongoing work together, the Lab plan gives a group shared cloud projects.","l":"studio/","t":"Open Studio","k":"share link send colleague supervisor collaborate copy project url"},{"q":"Does Lattent work offline?","a":"Yes. Choose Install app at the foot of any page (it shows the steps for your phone or computer) and Studio keeps analysing data without an internet connection, for example on an instrument computer. When you are online it always loads the latest version. Discover's database search and the AI chat need a connection.","l":"studio/","t":"Open Studio","k":"offline install app desktop internet connection pwa instrument computer without"},{"q":"Do I need to install anything?","a":"No. Lattent runs in a recent Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari with nothing to install and no account. You can also install it as an app for offline use: choose Install app at the foot of any page.","l":"studio/","t":"Open Studio","k":"install requirement requirements browser windows mac linux chrome firefox safari edge"},{"q":"Is Lattent free?","a":"Yes, for analysis: every analysis, model, tool and example is free without limits, and no account is needed. Pro adds publication exports, auto-written methods, batch runs and the AI chat; Lab covers a group. Current prices are on the pricing page.","l":"pricing/","t":"See pricing","k":"free cost price plan pro lab"},{"q":"How does Lattent compare with Origin or GraphPad Prism?","a":"Lattent is built around the measurements materials and chemistry labs make (XRD, spectra, band gaps, isotherms, Arrhenius data, tensile tests), with curve fitting, statistics and publication graphs underneath, plus a shape model, Bayesian optimisation and Facet. It runs in any browser with nothing to install and costs a fraction of a desktop licence. It does not yet do everything those programs do, such as 3D plots or two-way ANOVA.","l":"#faq","t":"Questions","k":"compare comparison versus origin prism graphpad excel igor matlab better different alternative"},{"q":"What is new in Lattent?","a":"Recent additions: Excel import, batch runs over many files, journal-size figure export, share by link, an installable offline app, and quick tools for adsorption kinetics, Tafel slopes and Avrami kinetics. The changelog lists every release.","l":"changelog/","t":"What's new","k":"new recent update updates release changelog latest version added"},{"q":"Which file formats can I import?","a":"Drag files onto Studio, or choose Import files to pick several at once. Lattent reads Excel workbooks (.xlsx, one table per sheet), CSV, TXT, DAT, XY, JCAMP-DX (.jdx, .dx, including compressed data), PANalytical .xrdml, Rigaku .ras, Bruker .uxd, Thermo/Galactic .spc and .cif. A CIF becomes a simulated XRD pattern. Binary vendor files (.raw, .brml, PerkinElmer .sp) and old .xls workbooks need saving in another format first. Nothing is uploaded.","l":"studio/","t":"Open Studio","k":"import file format excel xlsx xls spreadsheet batch many files csv jcamp jdx xrdml ras uxd spc cif raw drag drop upload instrument export"},{"q":"Why did the generator suggest this material?","a":"Press Why? next to any generated formula. It shows how often the diffusion model proposed it, its oxidation states, the predicted formation energy and band gap with 90% intervals, and an estimate of its distance from the convex hull built from Alexandria's stable phases in the same chemical system.","l":"studio/?discover=gen","t":"Generate materials","k":"why candidate explain generated convex hull stability decomposition suggestion reason"},{"q":"How do I cite Lattent?","a":"Use the Cite Lattent link in the footer or Studio's sidebar for BibTeX and APA references. If you used Discover, please also cite the Alexandria database and Matbench, listed in the same dialog.","l":"validation/","t":"Validation","k":"cite citation bibtex apa reference paper publish acknowledge"},{"q":"How accurate is the curve fitting?","a":"On the 52 NIST StRD nonlinear-regression reference fits, Lattent gets at least four correct significant digits in every parameter for 51 (median 8.6 digits); SciPy's curve_fit with default settings gets 45. The full benchmark is in the technical note on the Validation page.","l":"validation/#nist","t":"Technical note","k":"accuracy nist strd benchmark scipy curve_fit precision digits speed white paper"},{"q":"How do I identify the phases in my XRD pattern?","a":"Fit the peaks in Studio with X set to 2θ, then press Identify phases and list the elements that may be present. Lattent matches your peaks against every computed structure of those elements and flags peaks left unexplained.","l":"studio/?discover=phase","t":"Identify phases","k":"phase identification diffraction pattern xrd match crystal structure"},{"q":"How do I get the band gap from a UV–Vis spectrum?","a":"Paste wavelength (or energy) and absorbance into the band-gap tool. It builds the Tauc plot, finds the linear part of the absorption edge and reports the gap with a confidence interval.","l":"tools/band-gap-tauc/","t":"Band-gap tool","k":"tauc optical band gap uv vis absorbance edge"},{"q":"How do I get activation energy from conductivity or rate data?","a":"Use the activation-energy tool: paste temperature and conductivity (or rate constant) and Lattent fits Arrhenius or VFT and reports Eₐ in kJ/mol and eV with confidence intervals.","l":"tools/activation-energy-arrhenius/","t":"Activation-energy tool","k":"arrhenius activation energy conductivity rate temperature"},{"q":"Can Lattent suggest new materials?","a":"Yes, at the level of composition. The generator proposes formulas inside the elements you choose, steered towards a band gap, predicts stability and band gap with intervals, and checks each candidate against 5.8 million computed structures.","l":"studio/?discover=gen","t":"Generate materials","k":"generate new materials diffusion generative compositions discovery"},{"q":"Can Lattent write a report for me?","a":"Yes. Open Facet in Studio and choose Report. The agent plans the analyses, runs them, checks them for mistakes and assembles a report with methods, results, figures, checks and next steps. With your own AI key it also drafts the summary and discussion, and it can review figures you supply.","l":"studio/?example=anova&facet=report","t":"See an autonomous report","k":"report autonomous agent write up paper methods results export"},{"q":"Can Lattent read a graph from an image?","a":"Yes. In Facet, choose Graph: calibrate the axes with four clicks, click the curve, and Lattent traces it into a data table. With an AI key you can also attach the figure and ask what it shows or what is wrong with it.","l":"studio/?facet=graph","t":"Read a graph","k":"digitise digitize image plot picture figure graph data extract"},{"q":"What is Facet?","a":"Facet is Lattent’s AI lab partner. It suggests analyses, checks your project for mistakes, reads graphs, writes reports autonomously and, with your own Claude or GPT key, answers questions and reviews figures. All numbers come from the validated engine.","l":"ai/","t":"Facet AI","k":"facet ai assistant partner co-scientist"},{"q":"How much does Lattent cost?","a":"{{pricing}}","l":"pricing/","t":"See pricing","k":"price cost pro plan lab free subscription payment inr rupee"},{"q":"Is my data private?","a":"Analyses run in your browser and projects stay there, or in files you save. Nothing you paste is uploaded. The optional AI features send data only to the provider you chose, with your own key.","l":"legal/privacy.html","t":"Privacy notice","k":"privacy data upload security gdpr stored"},{"q":"How do I use an access code?","a":"If we sent you an access code (it starts with LAT-), open Account, find Licence key or access code, paste the code, enter the email address it was issued to and press Activate. Pro is then active on that browser; do the same on another computer with the same code. A code may carry an end date, and we can renew or withdraw it. Nothing is sent anywhere: the page checks the code against a fingerprint.","l":"account/","t":"Account and plans","k":"access code LAT- activate licence key free pro founder invitation unlock"},{"q":"How do I talk to a person?","a":"Use the contact form and tell us what you need. We usually reply within one working day.","l":"contact/","t":"Contact us","k":"contact email support human sales invoice question help"}];
